   "name": "Rational Expressions (Algebraic Fractions)",
   "definition": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Rational expressions"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What are rational expressions?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Rational** numbers are numbers that can be written as a fraction (**quotient**) Rational comes from **ratio** – a number is rational if it can be written as a ratio of two integers – ie a fraction!\n- A **rational** **expression** is an **algebraic** **fraction** The ratio between two algebraic expressions (usually polynomials)"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/06/2.6.1-Rational-Expressions-Notes-Diagram-1.png",
   "file": "assets/5752a30127b1-2-6-1-rational-expressions-notes-diagram-1.png",
   "alt": "Rational Expressions Notes Diagram 1, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I simplify rational expressions?"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2024/11/13236_rational-expression.png",
   "file": "assets/0b1a54e79d4f-13236-rational-expression.png",
   "alt": "Image",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- You may need to recall the **factor theorem**"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/06/2.6.1-Rational-Expressions-Notes-Diagram-2.png",
   "file": "assets/a74e499b0090-2-6-1-rational-expressions-notes-diagram-2.png",
   "alt": "Rational Expressions Notes Diagram 2, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Start by** factorising** polynomials using **factor** **theorem** or** algebraic** **division**"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "Simplify $\\frac{x^{3}-7x+6}{x^{2}+2x-3}$"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/06/2.6.1-Rational-Expressions-Notes-Diagram-3.png",
